Subject: skip tests subdir to avoid pygobject + python-dbusmock build deps
From:    Bero-OS batch 4
Date:    2026-05-12

accountsservice's tests/ subdir hard-requires python3 modules `gi` (PyGObject)
and `dbusmock`. These are heavy transitive deps that weren't worth chasing
just to compile a daemon we use at runtime (no test executions needed).

BLFS-recommended workaround is `mv tests/dbusmock{,-tests}` plus a sed, but
that still needs the Python modules to be installed. This patch removes the
subdir entirely, skipping all tests. accounts-daemon + libaccountsservice
still build and install.

Re-apply on rebuild from a clean tarball:
    cd /sources/accountsservice-23.13.9
    patch -p1 < /path/to/configs/patches/accountsservice-23.13.9-skip-tests-subdir.patch

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -232,7 +232,7 @@
   subdir('doc/libaccountsservice')
 endif

-subdir('tests')
+# subdir('tests')  # Bero-OS: tests need pygobject + python-dbusmock; skipped

 configure_file(
   output: 'config.h',
